      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Chevy Chase Land Company, founded in 1890 by Newlands and partners, acquired 1,700 acres that now stretch along Connecticut Avenue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chevy_Chase%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1894 the Land Company opened the Chevy Chase Spring Hotel, later renamed the Chevy Chase Inn, a social hub for early residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chevy_Chase%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area’s landscape mixes marshy lowlands shaped by the tidal Gunpowder River with forested uplands, creating diverse wetland and woodland habitats.",
